  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The Manual explains that the registered owner of a well-known trade mark can take infringement action against someone using, as a trade mark, a substantially identical or deceptively similar sign on unrelated goods or services.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part19B/4/4/2",
          "quote": "Under subsection 120(3), a registered owner of a well known trade mark can take infringement action against a person who uses, as a trade mark, a substantially identical or deceptively similar sign in relation to goods or services unrelated to those in respect of which the well known trade mark is registered."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "According to the Manual, the owner must establish that, because the trade mark is well known, use of the sign would likely indicate a connection between the unrelated goods or services and the registered owner.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part19B/4/4/2",
          "quote": "The registered owner will be required to establish that, because the trade mark is well known, use of the sign would be likely to be taken as indicating a connection between the unrelated goods or services and the registered owner"
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "The interests affected are the registered owner's: the Manual says the owner must also establish that those interests are likely to be adversely affected because of that perceived connection.",
      "quotes": [
        {
          "ref": "TMM/Part19B/4/4/2",
          "quote": "and for this reason the interests of the registered owner are likely to be adversely affected."
        }
      ],
      "authority": "manual"
    },
    {
      "text": "This account rests on the Manual's explanation of subsection 120(3); the supplied legislation does not include that subsection, so its full statutory requirements cannot be checked here.",
      "quotes": [],
      "authority": "none"
    }
  ],
